@@ -2215,6 +2215,14 @@ Entering pairing mode automatically makes the controller connectable,
 discoverable, and bondable. It also starts a yellow breathing LED pattern;
 leaving it restores the controller settings that were active beforehand.
 
+The restore follows the kernel's rule that `discoverable` requires
+`connectable` (`net/bluetooth/mgmt.c` rejects the visibility request while
+page scan is off): connectable is restored before discoverable, and
+discoverable is cleared before page scan is turned off. Pairing mode itself is
+always left, and its LED stopped, even if the controller refuses one of the
+restored settings; that failure is reported as an error by the `POST` and
+remains visible in `last_error` of `GET /api/v1/bluetooth`.
+
